  "body": "**Apply the quality-binding correction in #2984 before machine use or merge.** These offsets describe the measured resident selection. A colliding quality name can select a different process, so the effective recipe and its rough clearance require the corrected binding.\n\nStacked on #2955. Review the [height changes above the parent](https://github.com/qsmits/Camcraft/compare/6b790f4dd6aa0f4e37feeb03bd16b911fb19d664...4915595814341646b6d5e26160084754c5467b36).\n\nUse a measured rough-pass offset for each supported QN2 stock height. Apply it to the stock and corner clearance checks. Require the work to span the stock, with the work zero at its top. Unlisted heights and unsupported machine settings still refuse.\n\n| Stock height (mm) | Rough (mm) | Trim 1 (mm) | Trim 2 (mm) | Trim 3 (mm) |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| 15 | 0.245 | 0.155 | 0.140 | 0.134 |\n| 20 | 0.245 | 0.155 | 0.140 | 0.134 |\n| 40 | 0.260 | 0.170 | 0.140 | 0.130 |\n| 80 | 0.266 | 0.176 | 0.143 | 0.133 |\n\nThese are straight-face offsets from the native controller plot for the supported Berco Cut 0.25 mm wire, material and QN2 selection. The control owns the individual passes. Each new CAMCraft job produced eight plotted cut blocks including the 1 mm separation section. The threading hole and stock extended to the specified depth. The formal check reported no job error. The control requested machine and reference setup, and reported option 131072. No physical machine cut was made.\n\nThe 87 post library tests and all 10 native app integration tests passed. The app test qualified_qn2_heights_set_both_piece_and_work_with_stock_top_at_zero checks the stock and work Z spans. Strict Clippy passed for the app and post libraries.\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: Native Agie QN2 posting now accepts verified 15, 40 and 80 mm stock heights in addition to 20 mm. Corner checks use the measured rough-pass offset for the selected thickness.\n\nFixes #2954\n\n",
